\plain\\f3\\fs24  with \\plain\\cs18\\f3\\fs24 mild enlargement of the right ventricle\\plain\\f3\\fs24 , giving a right-sided cardiac contour.\\par\\line The \\plain\\cs18\\f3\\fs24 main pulmonary artery segment is enlarged \\plain\\f3\\fs24  and the \\plain\\cs18\\f3\\fs24 central pulmonary arteries are dilated\\plain\\f3\\fs24 . \\par There is \\plain\\cs18\\f3\\fs24 increased pulmonary vascularity\\plain\\f3\\fs24 , particularly in the upper lung fields, consistent with left-to-right shunt physiology.\\par\\line The lung fields are otherwise clear with no focal consolidation, pleural effusion, or pneumothorax.\\par\\line The bony thorax is unremarkable.\\par\\plain\\cs18\\f3\\fs24\\b\\i\\ul IMPRESSION:\\par\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\b\\i\\ul\\line\\plain\\f3\\fs24 Chest X-ray findings are \\plain\\cs18\\f3\\fs24 suggestive of an Atrial Septal Defect (ASD)\\plain\\f3\\fs24  \\par Correlation with \\plain\\cs18\\f3\\fs24 echocardiography\\plain\\f3\\fs24  is recommended for confirmation and assessment of defect type and shunt severity.\\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 13, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
