\\fs24 Fairly large rounded  soft tissue mass containing an air fluifd level is seen behind  the cardiac silhoutte .\\par\\plain\\f7\\fs24\\cf3 fundic gas shadow absent .\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sl360\\slmult1\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f7\\fs24\\ul\\cf3 IMPRESSION:\\plain\\f7\\fs24\\cf3   \\par\\plain\\f7\\fs22 Findings are compatible with hiatus hernia \\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b\\i widening of superior mediastinal contour is noted in the right side by a fairly large well defined soft tissue mass having convex outer margin whose medial margin merges with the mediastinum .\\par\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b\\i\\cf4\\cb5\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat5  Tracheal deviation to the left at the level of the thoracic outlet. \\par\\plain\\f6\\fs20\\b\\ul Impression:\\plain\\f6\\fs20  \\plain\\f6\\fs20\\b\\tab\\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par FINDINGS ARE SUSPICICOUS FOR A THYROID MASS   \\tab\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sl360\\slmult1\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080 CT SCAN IS ADVISED FOR FURTHER EVALUATION \\par\\pard\\s20\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sb134\\sa134\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b A \\plain\\cs21\\f6\\fs24\\b right upper lobe opacity\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b  with \\plain\\cs21\\f6\\fs24\\b volume loss\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b  is noted, showing a \\plain\\cs21\\f6\\fs24\\b concave inferior margin\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b  medially and a \\plain\\cs21\\f6\\fs24\\b convex contour\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b  laterally, giving the characteristic \\plain\\cs21\\f6\\fs24\\b\\loch\\f6\\hich\\f6\\\'93reverse S\\\'94 or \\\'93Golden S\\\'94 configuration\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b  of the minor fissure.\\line There is \\plain\\cs21\\f6\\fs24\\b hilar prominence\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b  on the right side, likely due to a \\plain\\cs21\\f6\\fs24\\b central mass lesion\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b  causing \\plain\\cs21\\f6\\fs24\\b lobar collapse\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b .\\line No pleural effusion or pneumothorax is seen.\\line Cardiac size and mediastinal contours are within normal limits.\\line Left lung field appears clear.\\line Bony thorax is unremarkable.\\par\\plain\\cs21\\f6\\fs24\\b\\ul Impression:\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b\\line Findings are consistent with \\plain\\cs21\\f6\\fs24\\b right upper lobe collapse secondary to a central obstructing mass lesion\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b  \\loch\\f6\\hich\\f6\\\'97 \\plain\\cs21\\f6\\fs24\\b\\loch\\f6\\hich\\f6\\\'93Golden S sign\\\'94\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b  positive.\\line Suggestive of \\plain\\cs21\\f6\\fs24\\b bronchogenic carcinoma\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b  until proven otherwise.\\line Further evaluation with \\plain\\cs21\\f6\\fs24\\b contrast-enhanced CT chest\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b  is advised.\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sl360\\slmult1\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\b\\cf3\\par\\pard\\s20\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\par\\par\\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f2\\fs20\\b\\tab  \\par\\pard\\s20\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sb134\\sa134\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\b There is a \\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24\\b well-defined / ill-defined soft tissue opacity\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\b  noted in the \\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24\\b superior mediastinum\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\b , more prominent on the \\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24\\b [right/left]\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\b  side.\\line The opacity causes \\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24\\b widening of the superior mediastinum\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\b  with \\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24\\b smooth / lobulated margins\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\b .\\line The \\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24\\b trachea is [central/deviated to the opposite side/slightly compressed]\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\b .\\line No evidence of calcification or air-fluid level is seen within the lesion.\\line Cardiac size and diaphragmatic outlines are normal.\\line Lung fields are clear with no pleural effusion or pneumothorax.\\line Bony thorax appears intact.\\par\\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24\\b\\ul Impression:\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\b\\line Features are suggestive of a \\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24\\b superior mediastinal mass lesion\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\b  \\loch\\f5\\hich\\f5\\\'97 possible \\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24\\b thymic, thyroidal, or lymph nodal\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\b  origin.\\line Further evaluation with \\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24\\b contrast-enhanced CT chest\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\b  is recommended for localization and characterization.\\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 13, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
