acture,dislocation or any other bone lesion is seen\\par\\plain\\f5\\fs12\\b\\par\\plain\\f5\\fs22 Articular margins are regular\\par\\plain\\f5\\fs12\\par\\plain\\f5\\fs22 Joint spaces are normal\\par\\plain\\f5\\fs12\\par\\plain\\f5\\fs22 Periarticular soft tissue appears normal\\par\\plain\\f5\\fs18\\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f5\\fs22\\b\\ul Comment\\plain\\f5\\fs22\\b : Normal finding.\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f8\\fs22\\\'b7\\tab}\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\fi-360\\li360\\tx360\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\ls1\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls1\\pnstart1\\pnf8\\pnfs22\\pnb\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}curvilinear avulsion fracture is seen at the site of medial collateral ligament consistent with a steida fracture .joint effusion noted .\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f8\\fs22\\\'b7\\tab}\\ls1\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls1\\pnstart1\\pnf8\\pnfs22\\pnb\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}T\\plain\\f6\\fs32\\cf3 ransverse fracture is seen through the midpole of the patella with displacement of the superior pole   and  the inferior pole by the patellar tendon. The result is marked\\plain\\f6\\fs22\\cf3  \\plain\\f6\\fs32\\cf3 distraction of the fragments  There is soft tissue swelling and a joint effusio\\plain\\f6\\fs22\\cf3 n\\plain\\f1\\fs22  \\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f5\\fs22\\b\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f8\\fs24\\\'b7 }\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\fi-360\\li360\\sb134\\sa134\\tx360\\ls2\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls2\\pnstart1\\pnf8\\pnfs24\\pnb\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}\\plain\\f4\\fs24 A \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 well-defined accessory ossicle\\plain\\f4\\fs24  is seen at the \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 superolateral aspect of the patella\\plain\\f4\\fs24 , separated from the main patellar body by a \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24  radiolucent cleft\\plain\\f4\\fs24 .The margins of both fragments are \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 smooth, rounded, and corticated\\plain\\f4\\fs24 ,\\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24\\b Bipartite patella\\plain\\f4\\fs24  \\plain\\f7\\fs24\\cf5 nly loc\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f2\\fs28\\b\\i\\ul The patella is fragmented but with smooth  corticated margins ,tripartite patella \\par\\plain\\f5\\fs22\\b\\tab Steida fracture \\par\\plain\\cs20\\f7\\fs20\\b\\cf6\\cb5\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat5\\tab\\plain\\cs20\\f7\\fs24\\b\\i\\cf6\\cb5\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat5 Pellegrini-Stieda lesion\\plain\\f7\\fs24\\b\\i\\cf6\\cb5\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat5\\loch\\f7\\hich\\f7\\~\\plain\\f7\\fs20\\cf6\\cb5\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat5\\par\\plain\\f2\\fs28 A displaced  curvilinear fracture  fragment is seen along the lateral tibial plateau corresponding with segond fracture \\par Soft tissue swelling is seen at the fractured site .\\plain\\f2\\fs28\\b\\i\\par\\plain\\f2\\fs36\\b Segond Fracture \\par\\plain\\f5\\fs22\\b  A well circumscribed lytic lesion with a narrow zone of transition and thin sclerotioc margin is seen in the metaphyseal region of  tibia .\\par No periosteal reaction or soft tissue component is noted .\\par\\plain\\f5\\fs22\\b\\ul Comment\\plain\\f5\\fs22\\b : Lytic lesion in the proximal tibial metaphyseal region ,possibly SBC,simple bone cyst \\plain\\f1\\fs22  \\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f2\\fs28\\b\\ul\\par\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f7\\fs20\\cf6\\cb7\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat7 The Klein line is drawn along the lateral aspect of the femoral neck and should intersect a portion of the lateral capital epiphysis.\\plain\\f4\\fs24  \\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\b\\cf6\\cb7\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat7  slipped upper femoral epiphysis.\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 13, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
