a crescent-shaped extra-axial hyperdense   hypodense  collection  is noted \\par\\par along the  right cerebral convexity, involving the right fronto parietal regions.\\par\\par  Effacement of adjacent cortical sulci is noted. \\par\\par Mass effect is evident as  midline shift seen on the left side .\\par\\par No clear intraparenchymal hemorrhage identified . \\par\\par\\par\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f4\\fs24 Generalized cerebral atrophy is evident by dilatation of  extracerebral CSF spaces .\\par\\par mild dilatation of  ventricles is noted .\\par\\par Corpus callosum & thalamus appear normal.\\par\\par Sella and pituitary are normal. Parasellar structures are unremarkable.\\par\\par There are no abnormalities in the cerebellopontine angle areas on both sides.\\par\\par The orbital contents are unremarkable. \\par\\par There are no abnormalities in the calvarium.\\par\\par\\par\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sb134\\sa134\\plain\\cs20\\f3\\fs24\\b\\ul Impression:\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\\'b7 }\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\fi-360\\li360\\ls1\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls1\\pnstart1\\pnf5\\pnfs24\\pnb0\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\b\\i  \\plain\\cs20\\f3\\fs24\\b\\i ACUTE SUB DURAL HEAMATOMA  IN THE RIGHT CERBREAL HEMISPHERE INTHE RIGHT FRONTOPARIETAL REGIONS \\plain\\f3\\fs24\\b\\i . \\par\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f3\\fs28\\b\\i\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f5\\fs28\\\'b7 }\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\fi-360\\li360\\ls2\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls2\\pnstart1\\pnf5\\pnfs28\\pnb\\pni\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}Age compatible  generalized cerebral atrophy \\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 1, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('ct chest ', '<p align="CENTER"><b><i><u><font size="4">REPORT</font></u></i></b></p><p align="JUSTIFY">&nbsp;</p><p align="JUSTIFY"><font face="Arial Narrow"><b><u>Clinical Information:</u> </b> Asthma ,chest pain .</font></p><p align="JUSTIFY">&nbsp;</p><p align="JUSTIFY"><font face="Arial Narrow"><b>Imaging Protocol: </b>Multiple Imaging sequences were realized in different planes. </font></p><p align="JUSTIFY"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><b>Findings:</b></font></font></p><ul>	<li>	<ul>		<li><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">The lung parenchyma shows normal attenuation. No focal lesion observed. Bronchovasacular markings are normal.</font></font></li>	</ul>	<ul>		<li><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">The mediastinum is centered and of normal width .</font></font></li>	</ul>	<ul>		<li><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">Hilar and perihilar region revealed no abnormality. Major intrathoraxic vessels and imaged portions of the supra aortic vessels are of normal size.</font></font></li>	</ul>	<ul>		<li><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">The heart is orthotropic with normal configuration .</font></font></li>	</ul>	<ul>		<li><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">The cardiac chambers are of normal size.</font></font></li>	</ul>	<ul>		<li><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">No pleural effusion observed.</font></font></li>	</ul>	<ul>		<li><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">No detectable lymphadenopathy.</font></font></li>	</ul>	<ul>		<li><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">Both domes of diaphragm are normal in position and smooth in outline. </font></font></li>	</ul>	<ul>		<li><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">The thoracic cage revealed no abnormality. The tracheal outline appears normal.</font></font></li>	</ul>	<ul>		<li><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4">Visualized liver revealed no abnormality.</font></font></li>	</ul>	</li></ul><p align="JUSTIFY">&nbsp;</p><p align="JUSTIFY"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><u><b>Impression :</b></u> <b> Normal findings</b></font></font><b><font face="Garamond" size="4"><font face="Garamond" size="4">.</font></font></b><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"> </font></font></p>', 'html', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 1, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('D-L Spine Normal', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff0{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\plain\\f0\\fs24 MRI REPORT OF DORSAL SPINE\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc Thanks for your referral\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par Clinical information:\\par Back pain.\\par\\par Technique: \\par Multiple imaging sequences were performed at different planes without contrast.\\par\\par Findings: \\par Dorsal kyphosis is slightly straightened with normal vertebral alignment.\\par Dorsal discs are of normal signal intensity.\\par Bone marrow and intrinsic cord signal intensities are within normal limit. \\par The vertebral bodies are normal in their number shape and interrelationship. \\par The articulating vertebral end plates present smooth margins. \\par The intervertebral disc spaces are of normal height and the discs do not project past the posterior surface of the vertebral bodies in any segment. \\par The spinal cord displays normal course, configuration, width and internal structure. \\par The Prevertebral and paravertebral soft tissue shows no abnormalities. \\par\\par Impression: \\par MRI of dorsal spine sows no definite abnormality.\\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('C-S  Spine - Deg', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff0{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\b\\ul MRI of cervical  spine\\par\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f0\\fs24 Sequences used: T1 and T2W Axial and sagittal images\\par Clinical History: Neck pain .\\par   \\par Finding:\\par Cervical lordosis is slightly straightened with forward subluxation of C4 over C5 . \\par Cervical discs are hypointense on T2WI due to reduced hydration. \\par No soft tissue abnormality is seen in neck.\\par\\par Altered signa intensity is seen in C6. \\par High signal intensity is seen in T2-STIR images in cervical cord at C5 level\\par Cervico medullary and cranio vertebral junction appears normal.\\par\\par\\par\\par At C4-5 level : Disc height is reduced. Retropulsed body of C5 is causing ventral thecal sac indentation, cord compression and bilateral neural foraminal narrowing. \\par\\par\\par Impression: \\par Degenerative disc disease.\\par Cervical spondylolisthesis at C4-5 level \\par Compressive myelopathy at C5 level.\\par Retropulsed body of C5 is causing thecal sac indentation , cord compression and bilateral neural foraminal narrowing at C4-5  level \\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('C-S  Disc disease', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff0{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\b\\ul MRI Cervical report\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par\\par\\par Technique: Multiple imaging sequences were realized in different planes.\\par Clinical information:  Neck pain\\par Findings:\\par\\loch\\f0\\hich\\f0\\\'95\\tab Cervical lordosis is straightened with normal vertebral alignment.\\par\\\'95\\tab All the cervical disc are normally hydrated evidenced by hyperintensity on T2WI. \\par\\\'95\\tab Cervical discs are hypointense on T2WI due to reduced hydration.\\par\\\'95\\tab No soft tissue abnormality is seen in neck.\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\\'95\\tab Bone marrow and intrinsic cord signal intensities are within normal limits.\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\\'95\\tab Craniovertebral and cervicomedullary junctions appear normal.\\par\\\'95\\tab Image pre & paravertebral region appear unremarkable. \\par\\\'95\\tab At C3-4, C4-5 & C5-6 levels: Circumferential disc bulge is causing corresponding thecal sac indentation and bilateral neural foraminal narrowing. \\par\\par Impression:\\par 1.\\tab Degenerative disc disease.\\par 2.\\tab Thecal sac indentation and bilateral neural foraminal narrowing at C3-4, C4-5 & C5-6 levels due to circumferential disc bulge. \\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('C-S  Miltipla diseases', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff0{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\plain\\f0\\fs24 MRI REPORT OF CERVICAL SPINE\\par         Thanks for your referral\\par\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par Clinical information:\\par\\par H/O neck pain radiates to left upper limb.\\par\\par Technique: \\par Multiple imaging sequences were performed at different planes without contrast.\\par\\par Findings: \\par\\par Cervical lordosis is straightened with normal vertebral alignment. \\par Cervical discs are hypointense (except at C7-D1 level) on T2WI due to reduced hydration. \\par No soft tissue abnormality is seen in neck. \\par Bone marrow and intrinsic cord signal intensities are within normal limit. \\par Cervico- medullary and cranio vertebral junction appears normal. \\par\\par At C2-3 level : Posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis with abutting disc are causing corresponding thecal sac indentation and narrowing of bilateral neural foramina.\\par\\par At C3-4 level: Posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis with abutting disc are causing corresponding thecal sac indentation and narrowing of bilateral neural foramina.\\par\\par At C4-5 level: Posterior contained disc herniation with mild posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis are causing corresponding thecal sac indentation and narrowing of bilateral neural foramina\\par At C5-6 level:  Posterior contained disc herniation with mild posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis are causing corresponding thecal sac indentation and narrowing of bilateral neural foramina.\\par At C6-7 level : Posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis with abutting disc are causing corresponding thecal sac indentation and narrowing of bilateral neural foramina.\\par\\par\\par Impression: \\par\\par Disco vertebral degenerative disease. \\par Thecal sac indentation with narrowing of bilateral neural foramina at C4-5 & C5-6 levels due to posterior contained disc herniation with mild posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis at these levels as stated. \\par Thecal sac indentation with narrowing of bilateral neural foramina at C2-3, C3-4 & C6-7 levels due to posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis with abutting disc at the respective levels as stated above. \\par\\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('L/S- Disc disease', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff0{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\b\\ul MRI REPORT OF LUMBAR SPINE\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\par       Thanks for your referral\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par Clinical information:\\par H/O low back pain 04 yrs, tingling and numbness at all limbs. \\par Technique: \\par Multiple imaging sequences were performed at different planes without contrast.\\par Findings: \\par Lumbar lordosis is straightened with normal vertebral alignment.\\par On T2 weighted images lumbar discs are hypointense due to disc desiccation.\\par Vertebrae show normal marrow signal intensities.\\par Visualized part of the cord appears normal in signal characteristics & morphology.\\par Images pre & paravertebral soft tissue appear normal.\\par\\par At L1-2 level: Posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis with abutting disc are causing corresponding thecal sac indentation and narrowing of bilateral neural foramina. \\par At  L2-3 level: Posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis with abutting disc are causing corresponding thecal sac indentation and narrowing of bilateral neural foramina. \\par At L3-4 level: Posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis with abutting disc and hypertrophied facet are causing corresponding thecal sac indentation and narrowing of bilateral neural foramina. \\par At L4-5 level: Posterior & posterolateral contained disc herniation with mild posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis and hypertrophied facet are causing corresponding thecal sac indentation and narrowing of bilateral neural foramina\\par At L5-S1 level: Posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis with abutting disc and hypertrophied facet are causing corresponding epidural fat indentation and narrowing of bilateral neural foramina. \\par Screening MRI of cervico-dorsal spine shows disc osteophyte complex at multiple cervical levels. \\par Impression:\\par Disco vertebral degenerative disease. \\par Thecal sac indentation with narrowing of bilateral neural foramina at L4-5 level due to posterior & posterolateral contained disc herniation with mild posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis and hypertrophied facet at the same level as stated. \\par Thecal sac / epidural fat indentation with narrowing of bilateral neural foramina at L1-2, L2-3, L3-4 & L5-S1 levels: Posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis with abutting disc with or without  hypertrophied facet at the respective levels as stated. \\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('Brain - Normal', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff0{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\par\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\b\\ul MRI REPORT OF BRAIN\\par\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\par Thanks for your referral\\par\\par\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar Clinical information: Headache and vertigo.\\par\\par Technique : Multiple imaging sequences were performed at different planes without contrast.\\par\\par Findings :\\par On DWI no area of increased signal intensity or restricted diffusion is noted to suggest any recent infarct or other compatible pathology.\\par Gray white matter signal intensities are within normal limits.\\par Pituitary, parasellar areas, corpus callosum, optic chiasma, thalami, basal ganglia and cerebellum appear normal in signal characteristics and morphology. \\par Midline structures are not shifted. \\par Cerebrum and cerebellum show normal cortical sulcations. \\par Ventricles are of normal size and symmetrical with normal CSF flow. \\par Both CP angles are clear. \\par Normal basal flow voids are seen. \\par Visualized cranial nerves appear normal. \\par Orbits are unremarkable. \\par Paranasal sinuses show no significant mucosal thickening.\\par\\par Impression:\\par MRI of brain reveals no definite abnormality.\\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('MRCP- Acute Pancreatic', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff0{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\plain\\f0\\fs24 MRI REPORT OF MRCP\\par\\par Thanks for your referral\\par\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par Clinical information:\\par Upper abdominal pain.\\par Anorexia and nausea.\\par\\par Technique: \\par\\par 2D breath hold MR hydrography was done to realize MRCP\\par\\par Findings: \\par\\par The common bile duct shows normal position, caliber and length with a homogeneous fluid equivalent intraluminal signal.\\par\\par The cystic duct and images portions of the intrahepatic bile duct also appear normal.\\par\\par The gall bladder is of normal size. It has smooth borders and homogeneous contents.\\par\\par The pancreatic duct is prominent.\\par Supply MRI snows slightly swollen pancreas. \\par\\par\\par Impression: \\par Acute on chronic pancreatitis.\\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('L/S- Deg', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff0{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\plain\\f0\\fs24 Thank you for your kind referral\\par\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\b\\ul  MRI report of Lumbar spine\\par\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\par\\par\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar Sequences used: T1 and T2W Axial and sagittal images\\par Clinical History: Low back pain.\\par Findings:      \\par Lumbar lordosis is slightly straightened with normal vertebral alignment \\par On T2 weighted images L3-4 and L4-5 lmbar  discs are hypointense due to reduced hydration/ disc desiccation \\par Modic type II degenerative end plates are seen in L3,L4, evidenced by T1 and T2 hyperintensity signals\\par The rest of vertebrae show normal marrow signal intensities.\\par Visualised part of the cord appear normal in signal characteristics and morphology.\\par Imaged pre & paravertebral soft tissue appears normal. \\par\\par At L3-4 level: Posterolateral osteophytosis with abutting disc are causing bilateral neural foraminal narrowing.\\par\\par At L4-5 level: Broad-based posterior  disc bulge with mild posterolateral osteophytosis& facet hypertrophy are causing thecal sac indentation   and bilateral neural foraminal narrowing.\\par\\par Screening of rest of spine reveals disc desiccation with variable disc height in cervical region.\\par\\par\\par Impression :\\par\\loch\\f0\\hich\\f0\\\'95\\tab Degenerative disc disease. \\par\\\'95\\tab Thecal sac indenation  with bilateral  neural foraminal narrowing at L4-5  level due to disc bulge,  osteophytosis & facet hypertrophy \\par\\\'95\\tab Bilateral neural foraminal narrowing at L3-4 level due to posterolateral osteophytosis with abutting disc\\par  \\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('Knee- ACL Tear', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff0{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\b\\ul MRI REPORT OF   LEFT KNEE JOINT \\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\par Clinical history : Trauma to knee  joint \\par Technique : Multiple axial , coronal and sagittal T1,T2 and STIR images are shown  \\par Findings :\\par Moderate  joint effusion is noted as evidenced by increased area of fluid signal intensities in both the gutters of the supra-patellar bursa and intra-articular joint space.\\par ACL is not visualized \\par PCL shows high signal ingensity in its femoral attachement \\par Verticla hyperintensity is seen in posterior horn of medial meniscus communicating with both articular surfaces.\\par Lateral meniscus is unremarkable \\par The bones comprising the knee joint show normal configuration and position.\\par The cortex show smooth contours and normal thickness . \\par High signal intensity is seen in subchondral location of posterior aspect of medial tibial condyle.\\par The cartilage covering the patella, femoral condyles, and tibial plateaus is of normal thickness and has normal signal characteristics. \\par The cartilaginous surface is smooth. \\par The collateral ligaments are intact and of normal width.\\par The soft tissues surrounding the knee joint are edematous .\\par\\par\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\b\\ul Impression:\\par\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\par Moderate jont effusion .\\par ACL tear\\par Intrasubstance tear of PCL in femoral attachment \\par Vertical tear of posterior horn of medial meniscus.\\par Contusion in medial condyle of  tibia . \\par Soft tissue injury .\\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('MRI- Chest', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff0{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\plain\\f0\\fs24 MRI OF CHEST\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par Brief clinical notes :\\tab Pain in chest.\\par\\par Technique : Multiple sequences were obtained in axial and coronal planes.\\par\\par Findings : \\par\\par A welldefined SOL measuring 7.6cmx7.6cmx12.6cm is noted in posterior part of left hemithorx. The structure shows a cystic character, hypointense on T1 and Hyperintense on T2. Sediments are noted in the dependent part. The rim is clean and sharp. Left lower lobe is collapsed.\\par Right lung is normally aerated and applied to the chest wall on all sides. The pleurae show normal homogeneous signal intensity and there are not fluid collections. \\par The pulmonary structures are normal and presents normal vascular markings. There are no intrapulmonary nodules or patchy densities. \\par The mediastinum is centered and of normal width. There is no evidence of masses in the anterior, central or posterior compartment. \\par The hilar region on right side is unremarkable and the main bronchi appear normal. There is no lymphadenopathy and there are no perihilar masses on either side.\\par The heart is orthotopic and has a normal configuration. The cardiac chambers are of normal size. Major intrathoracic vessels are unremarkable and imaged portions of the supra-aortic vessels appear normal. \\par The thoracic skeleton and thoracic soft tissues show no abnormalities.\\par\\par IMPRESSION : \\par\\par Suggestive of an encysted pleural effusion (Lt) /??cystic mass in left paravertebral gutter.\\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('MRCP- Normal', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff0{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\b\\ul MRCP REPORT \\par\\plain\\f0\\fs24          Thanks for your referral\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par Clinical information:\\par C/C - Abdominal pain\\par\\par Technique: \\par\\par 2D breath hold MR hydrography was done to realize MRCP\\par\\par Findings: \\par The common bile duct shows normal position, caliber and length with a homogeneous fluid equivalent intraluminal signal.\\par\\par The cystic duct and images portions of the intrahepatic bile duct also appear normal.\\par\\par The gall bladder is apears normal. It has smooth borders and homogeneous contents.\\par\\par The pancreatic duct shows normal position, length and caliber with homogeneous internal structure and smooth contours.\\par\\par Impression: \\par\\par Normal MRCP study.\\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('Knee- Mild Joint Effusion', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff0{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f0\\fs24 MRI OF RIGHT KNEE JOINT\\par\\par\\par\\par Brief clinical notes : \\par\\par Technique : Multiple sequences were performed in different planes.\\par\\par Findings : \\par\\par The anterior cruciate ligament the posterior cruciate ligament is intact.\\par\\par Lateral meniscus is intact in form and signal.\\par\\par Posterior horn of medial meniscus is showing high signal intensity change communicating to superior & inferior articular margin.\\par\\par Visible bones revealed no abnormal signal.\\par\\par The medial and lateral collateral ligaments are intact. \\par The extensor mechanism is intact. \\par\\par Mild joint effusion is noted. \\par\\par Impression :\\par\\par 1.\\tab Tear of posterior horn of medial meniscus.\\par 2.\\tab Mild joint effusion. \\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('Knee- Multiple Disease', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff0{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\b MRI REPORT OF LEFT KNEE JOINT\\par\\plain\\f0\\fs24         Thanks for your referral\\par\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par Clinical information:\\par\\par Left knee pain, difficulty to movement. \\par\\par Technique: \\par Multiple imaging sequences were performed at different planes without contrast.\\par\\par Findings: \\par\\par Mild joint effusion is noted as evidenced by increased area of fluid signal intensities in both the gutters of the supra-patellar bursa and intra-articular joint space. \\par Horizontal linear hyperintensity is noted in the posterior horn of the lateral meniscus.\\par Obli1que hyperintensity is noted in the posterior horn of the medial meniscus. \\par Altered signal intensity is noted along the course of MCL.\\par The bones comprising the knee joint show normal configuration and position. \\par The bone marrow signal is normal, with a normal trabecular pattern and normal epiphyseal lines. \\par The cortex show smooth contours and normal thickness with no sub-chondral signal changes. \\par The cartilage covering the patella, femoral condyles, and tibial plateaus is of normal thickness and has normal signal characteristics. \\par The cartilaginous surface is smooth. \\par Anterior and posterior cruciate ligaments are intact and are normal in their width and signal characteristics. \\par The soft tissue surrounding the knee joint shows mild hyperintensities on STIR images, suggesting mild soft tissue injury\\par Popliteal cyst is noted over and under the medial head of the gestrocnemious. \\par\\par\\par Impression: \\par\\par Mild joint effusion. \\par Grade II signal change in the posterior horn of lateral meniscus with oblique tear in the posterior horn of medial meniscus.\\par MCL injury. \\par Popliteal cyst over and under the medial head of the gestrocnemious. \\par Mild soft tissue injury. \\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('MRI Shoulder', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff0{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\b\\ul MRI OF RIGHT SHOULDER JOINT\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\par Thanks for your referral\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qj Technique: Multiple axial ,coronal , sagitteal images are taken in different sequences.\\par Clinical notes : Pain \\par Findings :\\par A depressed area is seen in posterosuperior humeral head \\par Moderate joint effusion is seen with extension in to inferoglenohumeral recess \\par High signal intensity is seen in base of superior labrum\\par high signal intnesity is seen at the attachment of supraspinatus tendon\\par The acromioclavicular joint has normal configuration, but containing mild fluid.\\par Collection is also seen in subacromial bursa\\par Glenoid cavity and adjacent scapula shows hight signal intensity with hight signal intensity in triceps muscle . \\par The other muscles that cover the shoulder joint appear normal, as do imaged portions of the lung and soft tissues. \\par\\par\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\b Impression :\\par\\plain\\f0\\fs24 ?Hill-Sachs deformity \\par Injury to glenoid cavity with adjacent scapula\\par ?Avulsion fracture at the site of supraspinatus tendon\\par Moderate joint effusion \\par ?Superior labral and inferoglenohumeral ligament injury \\par Triceps muscle injury .\\par\\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('MRI CERVICAL SPINE ', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff1{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\fswiss\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Calibri;}\r\n{\\f2\\froman\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Times New Roman;}\r\n{\\f3\\fswiss\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial Black;}\r\n{\\f4\\fswiss\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial Narrow;}\r\n{\\f5\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\widctlpar\\sa200\\sl276\\slmult1\\f1\\fs22 Normal;}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}{\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\s17\\itap0\\keepn\\widctlpar\\f2\\fs40\\sbasedon0\\snext0 heading 1;}{\\s18\\itap0\\widctlpar\\f2\\fs26\\sbasedon0 Body Text;}{\\s19\\itap0\\widctlpar\\f2\\fs26\\b\\sbasedon0 Body Text 3;}}\r\n{\\*\\listtable{\\list\\listtemplateid1{\\listlevel\\levelnfc0\\leveljc0\\levelfollow0\\levelstartat1\\levelspace0\\levelindent0{\\leveltext\\\'02\\\'00.;}{\\levelnumbers\\\'01;}\\f4\\fs24\\b\\i0\\strike0\\ul0\\cf0\\cb0\\fi-360\\li360}{\\listlevel\\levelnfc0\\leveljc0\\levelfollow0\\levelstartat1\\levelspace0\\levelindent0{\\leveltext\\\'02\\\'01.;}{\\levelnumbers\\\'01;}\\f4\\fs24\\b\\i0\\strike0\\ul0\\cf0\\cb0\\fi-360\\li720}{\\listlevel\\levelnfc0\\leveljc0\\levelfollow0\\levelstartat1\\levelspace0\\levelindent0{\\leveltext\\\'02\\\'02.;}{\\levelnumbers\\\'01;}\\f4\\fs24\\b\\i0\\strike0\\ul0\\cf0\\cb0\\fi-360\\li1080}{\\listlevel\\levelnfc0\\leveljc0\\levelfollow0\\levelstartat1\\levelspace0\\levelindent0{\\leveltext\\\'02\\\'03.;}{\\levelnumbers\\\'01;}\\f4\\fs24\\b\\i0\\strike0\\ul0\\cf0\\cb0\\fi-360\\li1440}{\\listlevel\\levelnfc0\\leveljc0\\levelfollow0\\levelstartat1\\levelspace0\\levelindent0{\\leveltext\\\'02\\\'04.;}{\\levelnumbers\\\'01;}\\f4\\fs24\\b\\i0\\strike0\\ul0\\cf0\\cb0\\fi-360\\li1800}{\\listlevel\\levelnfc0\\leveljc0\\levelfollow0\\levelstartat1\\levelspace0\\levelindent0{\\leveltext\\\'02\\\'05.;}{\\levelnumbers\\\'01;}\\f4\\fs24\\b\\i0\\strike0\\ul0\\cf0\\cb0\\fi-360\\li2160}{\\listlevel\\levelnfc0\\leveljc0\\levelfollow0\\levelstartat1\\levelspace0\\levelindent0{\\leveltext\\\'02\\\'06.;}{\\levelnumbers\\\'01;}\\f4\\fs24\\b\\i0\\strike0\\ul0\\cf0\\cb0\\fi-360\\li2520}{\\listlevel\\levelnfc0\\leveljc0\\levelfollow0\\levelstartat1\\levelspace0\\levelindent0{\\leveltext\\\'02\\\'07.;}{\\levelnumbers\\\'01;}\\f4\\fs24\\b\\i0\\strike0\\ul0\\cf0\\cb0\\fi-360\\li2880}{\\listlevel\\levelnfc0\\leveljc0\\levelfollow0\\levelstartat1\\levelspace0\\levelindent0{\\leveltext\\\'02\\\'08.;}{\\levelnumbers\\\'01;}\\f4\\fs24\\b\\i0\\strike0\\ul0\\cf0\\cb0\\fi-360\\li3240}{\\listname ;}\\listid1}}\r\n{\\*\\listoverridetable{\\listoverride\\listid1\\listoverridecount0\\ls1}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12240\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\s17\\itap0\\keepn\\widctlpar\\qc\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f3\\fs26\\b\\ul MRI OF CERVICAL SPINE\\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\qj\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\par\\pard\\s17\\itap0\\keepn\\widctlpar\\qj\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b Brief clinical notes :\\plain\\f4\\fs24  Pain in Neck and right shoulder \\loch\\f4\\hich\\f4\\\'96 4 years. \\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\qj\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\par\\pard\\s18\\itap0\\widctlpar\\qj\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b Technique :\\plain\\f4\\fs24  A total of 4 sequences were performed consisting of T1Sagittal, T1 Axial, T2 sagittal, T2 Axial (5 sheets). \\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\qj\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\par\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b Findings : \\par\\plain\\f4\\fs24 Loss of cervical lordosis is noted. \\par Bodies of C4, C5 and C6 are slightly reduced in height. \\par\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080 The cervical cord is normal in location and appearance. No abnormality of the visualized paravertebral soft tissue is shown.    \\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\qj\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080  \\par\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b C2-C3 : \\plain\\f4\\fs24 Normal signal intensity is noted in the disc with normal disc height. Levels are unremarkable. \\par\\par\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b C3-C4 :\\plain\\f4\\fs24  Reduction of signal intensity with reduction of height is noted in the disc. Evidence of central and both paracentral annular disc bulge indenting ventral subarachnoid space Inter vertebral foramina of left side is a little narrowed. \\par\\par\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b C6-C5 :\\plain\\f4\\fs24  Reduction of signal intensity with reduction of height is noted in the disc. Evidence of central and both paracentral annular disc bulge indenting ventral subarachnoid space Inter vertebral foramina of both sides are narrowed. \\par\\par\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b C5-C6 :\\plain\\f4\\fs24  Reduction of signal intensity with reduction of height is noted in the disc. Evidence of central and both paracentral annular disc bulge indenting ventral subarachnoid space Inter vertebral foramina of both sides are narrowed. \\par\\par\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b C6-C7 & C7-T1 :\\plain\\f4\\fs24  Normal signal intensity is noted in the disc with normal disc height. Levels are unremarkable. \\par\\par\\par\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b\\ul IMPRESSION :\\par{\\listtext\\pard\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b\\ul 1.\\tab}\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\qj\\fi-360\\li360\\tx360\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\ls1\\ilvl0\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b Loss of cervical lordosis is noted. \\par{\\listtext\\pard\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b 2.\\tab}\\ls1\\ilvl0 Multilevel disc desiccation.\\par{\\listtext\\pard\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b 3.\\tab}\\ls1\\ilvl0 C3-C4 : Early disc desiccation. Central and both paracentral annular disc bulge indenting ventral subarachnoid space Inter vertebral foramina of left side is a little narrowed. \\par{\\listtext\\pard\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b 4.\\tab}\\ls1\\ilvl0 C4-C5 : Early disc desiccation. Central and both paracentral annular disc bulge Inter vertebral foramina of both sides are narrowed. \\par{\\listtext\\pard\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b 5.\\tab}\\ls1\\ilvl0 C5-C6 : Desiccated disc. Central and both paracentral annular disc bulge Inter vertebral foramina of both sides are narrowed. \\par{\\listtext\\pard\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b 6.\\tab}\\ls1\\ilvl0 C6-C7 & C7-T1 : Levels are unremarkable. \\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 2, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
