\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\sl360\\slmult1\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\b\\ul X-RAY CHEST (P.A  VIEW)\\par EXPIRATORY FILM \\par\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\\'b7\\tab}\\pard\\s18\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qj\\fi-360\\li720\\sl360\\slmult1\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\ls1\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls1\\pnstart1\\pnf6\\pnfs24\\pnb\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnul\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}\\plain\\f3\\fs24 Trachea is central in position\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\\'b7\\tab}\\ls1\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls1\\pnstart1\\pnf6\\pnfs24\\pnb0\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}Both lung fields are clear.\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\\'b7\\tab}\\ls1\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls1\\pnstart1\\pnf6\\pnfs24\\pnb0\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}Both domes of diaphragm are normal in contour and definition. \\plain\\f3\\fs24\\cf3\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\\'b7\\tab}\\pard\\s18\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qj\\fi-360\\li720\\sl360\\slmult1\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\ls2\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls2\\pnstart1\\pnf6\\pnfs24\\pnb0\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf3\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}Both CP angle are normal.\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\\'b7\\tab}\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qj\\fi-360\\li720\\sl360\\slmult1\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\ls2\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls2\\pnstart1\\pnf6\\pnfs24\\pnb0\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf3\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}\\plain\\f1\\fs28\\cf3 Heart size appear enlarged in transverse diameter maybe due to poor inspiration .\\plain\\f1\\fs24\\cf3\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\\'b7\\tab}\\ls2\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls2\\pnstart1\\pnf6\\pnfs24\\pnb0\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf3\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\cf3 Bony thorax appears normal.  \\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qj\\sl360\\slmult1\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\b\\cf3\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sl360\\slmult1\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\b\\ul\\cf3 IMPRESSION:\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\b\\cf3   \\par\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f6\\fs24\\\'b7\\tab}\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qj\\fi-360\\li720\\sl360\\slmult1\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\ls3\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls3\\pnstart1\\pnf6\\pnfs24\\pnb\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf3\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\b As per description\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\b\\cf4\\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 13, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('SHOULDER CT ', '<p><font size="4"><font size="4"><font face="Times New Roman"><b>Brief Clinical Notes:RTA</b> </font></font></font></p><p align="JUSTIFY">&nbsp;</p><p align="JUSTIFY"><font size="4"><font size="4"><font face="Times New Roman"><b>Technique: </b>Volume axial scan of shoulder bone was done. Axial, sagittal and coronal images are shown in the films.</font></font></font></p><p align="JUSTIFY"><font size="4"><font size="4"><font face="Times New Roman"><b>Findings:</b> </font></font></font></p><p align="JUSTIFY">&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p align="JUSTIFY">&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><ol>	<li>	<ul>		<li><font size="4"><font size="4"><font face="Times New Roman">There is comminuted fracture through the surgical neck of humerus extending into the greater and lesser tuberosities with displacement and angulation of humeral head .</font></font></font></li>	</ul>	<ul>		<li><font size="4"><font size="4"><font face="Times New Roman">The fracture fragments involve as per the neer classification of humeral head fracture includes : </font></font></font></li>	</ul>	</li></ol><p align="JUSTIFY"><font size="4"><font size="4"><font face="Times New Roman">the humeral head ,greater tuberosity ,lesser tuberosity and humeral shaft .</font></font></font></p><p align="JUSTIFY">&nbsp;</p><p align="JUSTIFY"><font size="4"><font size="4"><font face="Times New Roman"></font></font></font></p><p align="JUSTIFY"><font size="4"><font size="4"><font face="Times New Roman">3. There is displacement of more than 1 cm of involved fractured fragments noted .</font></font></font></p><p align="JUSTIFY"><font size="4"><font size="4"><font face="Times New Roman">4. There is also associated anterior inferior dislocation of humeral head .</font></font></font></p><p align="JUSTIFY"><font size="4"><font size="4"><font face="Times New Roman">5. No other associated injuries are seen at the acromiovclavicular joint,scapula or the clavicle .</font></font></font></p><p align="JUSTIFY">&nbsp;</p><p align="JUSTIFY"><font size="4"><font size="4"><b><font face="Times New Roman">Impression: </font></b></font></font></p><p><font size="4"><font size="4"><b><font face="Times New Roman">CT findings are compatible with displaced comminuted 3 parts fracture of proximal humerus involving the surgical neck, greater tuberosity,anatomical neck ( according to neer classification ), with anterior inferior dislocation of head of humerus .</font></b></font></font></p><p><b><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><img height="75" src="http://teleradbangladesh.selfip.com/Image1.gif" width="174" /></font></font></b></p>', 'html', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 1, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
