0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\par\\par\\pard\\s23\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sb93\\sa186\\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs28\\b Findings:\\plain\\f5\\fs28\\b\\par\\pard\\s22\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sb134\\sa134\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\loch\\f5\\hich\\f5\\\'95 A fracture line is seen involving the\\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24   distal fibula\\par\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\line\\loch\\f5\\hich\\f5\\\'95 \\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24 Adjacent soft tissue swelling\\plain\\f5\\fs24  is noted around the ankle.\\par\\line\\loch\\f5\\hich\\f5\\\'95 Joint space is \\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24 preserved \\par\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\line\\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24\\b\\i\\ul Impression:\\plain\\f5\\fs24\\b\\i\\par\\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24 Fracture at the  distal fibula \\par\\pard\\s18\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sb60\\sa120\\sl480\\slmult1\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\tx10800\\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24\\b fragmentation  and increased density\\plain\\f1\\fs22\\b  of the calcaneal apophysis is noted. compared with the adjacent calcaneal body.\\par\\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24\\b\\i\\ul Impression:\\plain\\f1\\fs22\\b\\i\\ul\\line\\plain\\f1\\fs22 Radiographic features are \\plain\\cs21\\f5\\fs24 suggestive of calcaneal apophysitis (Sever disease)\\plain\\f1\\fs22  \\plain\\f3\\fs28\\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 13, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('mri degenerative doisc herniation ', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff1{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\fswiss\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Calibri;}\r\n{\\f2\\fswiss\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f3\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\widctlpar\\f1\\fs22 Normal;}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}{\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12240\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qc\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\b\\ul MRI REPORT OF LUMBAR SPINE\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\par       Thanks for your referral\\par\\pard\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\par Clinical information:\\par H/O low back pain radiating to both lower limbs .\\par . \\par Technique: \\par Multiple imaging sequences were performed at different planes without contrast.\\par\\par Findings: \\par\\par\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\b\\ul Sagittal level\\par\\par\\plain\\f2\\fs24 Lumbar lordosis is straightened with normal vertebral alignment.\\par On T2 weighted images lumbar discs are hypointense due to disc desiccation.\\par The disc heights are reduced at L1-L2,L2-L3 and L3-L4  intervertebral levels .\\par Type 11 modic changes are seen in the L3- L4 VertebraL bodies.\\par Visualized part of the cord appears normal in signal characteristics & morphology\\par The conus terminates at the inferior aspect of L1 vertebral body and has a normal appearance .\\par Images pre & paravertebral soft tissue appear normal.\\par\\par\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\b\\ul Axial level :\\par\\par\\plain\\f2\\fs24 At L1-2 level: Posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis with right paracentral disc prutrusion  are causing corresponding thecal sac indentation.\\par\\par At  L3-L4 level: Broad based Central and left paracentral   disc herniation with caudal migration and posterior and  posteriolateral  osteophytosis,facet arthrosis and flaval hypertrophy are causing mild canal stenosis and bilateral neural foraminal narrowing with compression of L4 nerve root on left side .  \\par\\par At L4-L5 level: Broad based Central and left paracentral disc herniation with caudal migration and  Posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis ,facet arthrosis   and flaval hypertrophy  are causing corresponding canal stenosis and effacement of lateral recesses and  bilateral neural foraminal narrowing with compression of traversing L5 nerve root on left side . . \\par\\par At L5-S1 level:Broad based posterior and posteriolateral disc herniation ,Posterior & posterolateral osteophytosis and  hypertrophied facet are causing corresponding epidural fat indentation and narrowing of bilateral neural foramina. \\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 1, '2024-06-12 05:56:25');
