\\b\\i\\ul\\cf5\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6 diaphyseal region of ulna .The buttherfly fragm\\plain\\f1\\fs22\\b\\i\\ul\\cf5\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6 ent \\plain\\f2\\fs28\\b\\i\\ul  has mild lateral angulation and displacement  \\par\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\tx1134\\tx2268\\tx3402\\tx4536\\tx5670\\tx6804\\tx7938\\tx9072\\tx10206\\tx11340\\tx12474\\tx13608\\tx14742\\tx15876\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f2\\fs28 Fractures are seen at the mid shafts of both radius and ulna .\\par\\par Joints spaces are normal. \\par\\par Articular margins are regular in out line. \\par\\par Soft tissue swelling is seen around the fractured site .\\par\\plain\\f2\\fs32\\b\\par\\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\tx1134\\tx2268\\tx3402\\tx4536\\tx5670\\tx6804\\tx7938\\tx9072\\tx10206\\tx11340\\tx12474\\tx13608\\tx14742\\tx15876\\plain\\f2\\fs36\\b Comment: Fractures at the mid shafts of both radius and ulna .\\plain\\f5\\fs22  \\par\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sb134\\sa134\\tx1134\\tx2268\\tx3402\\tx4536\\tx5670\\tx6804\\tx7938\\tx9072\\tx10206\\tx11340\\tx12474\\tx13608\\tx14742\\tx15876\\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 Oblique fracture:\\plain\\f4\\fs24 Fracture line runs \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 diagonally across the bone shaft\\plain\\f4\\fs24 .Typically a \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 single straight diagonal line\\plain\\f4\\fs24  from one cortex to the opposite.\\par\\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 Spiral fracture:\\plain\\f4\\fs24 Fracture line \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 wraps around the bone like a corkscrew\\plain\\f4\\fs24 .Often appears \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 helical on radiographs\\plain\\f4\\fs24 .Caused by \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 torsional (twisting) force\\plain\\f4\\fs24 .\\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\tx1134\\tx2268\\tx3402\\tx4536\\tx5670\\tx6804\\tx7938\\tx9072\\tx10206\\tx11340\\tx12474\\tx13608\\tx14742\\tx15876\\par }', 'r