\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}\\plain\\f4\\fs22  \\plain\\f4\\fs24 Fibro-nodular opacities are seen predominantly in the \\plain\\cs21\\f4\\fs24 upper lobes\\plain\\f4\\fs24 , more marked on the \\plain\\cs21\\f4\\fs24 right side\\plain\\f4\\fs24 .\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f8\\fs24\\\'b7 }\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\fi-360\\li360\\sb134\\sa134\\ls2\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls2\\pnstart1\\pnf8\\pnfs24\\pnb0\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}\\plain\\cs21\\f4\\fs24 Patchy areas of consolidation\\plain\\f4\\fs24  and \\plain\\cs21\\f4\\fs24 ill-defined nodular infiltrates\\plain\\f4\\fs24  are noted within these regions.\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f8\\fs24\\\'b7 }\\ls2\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls2\\pnstart1\\pnf8\\pnfs24\\pnb0\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}Presence of \\plain\\cs21\\f4\\fs24 cavitary lesions\\plain\\f4\\fs24  with irregular thick walls noted in the right upper lobe \\loch\\f4\\hich\\f4\\\'97 suggestive of \\plain\\cs21\\f4\\fs24 active caseation\\plain\\f4\\fs24 .\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f8\\fs24\\\'b7 }\\ls2\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls2\\pnstart1\\pnf8\\pnfs24\\pnb0\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}Adjacent \\plain\\cs21\\f4\\fs24 fibrotic strands\\plain\\f4\\fs24  and \\plain\\cs21\\f4\\fs24 volume loss\\plain\\f4\\fs24  are present with \\plain\\cs21\\f4\\fs24 superior retraction of the hilum and horizontal fissure\\plain\\f4\\fs24 .\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f8\\fs24\\\'b7 }\\ls2\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls2\\pnstart1\\pnf8\\pnfs24\\pnb0\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}\\plain\\cs21\\f4\\fs24 Bronchiectatic changes\\plain\\f4\\fs24  noted within the fibrotic zones.\\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f8\\fs24\\\'b7 }\\ls2\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls2\\pnstart1\\pnf8\\pnfs24\\pnb0\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}No significant pleural effusion or pneumothorax.\\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\cs21\\f4\\fs24 Cardiac silhouette and bony thorax\\plain\\f4\\fs24  appear unremarkable.\\par\\plain\\cs21\\f4\\fs24\\b\\ul\\par Impression:\\par\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\line\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b Features are suggestive of \\plain\\cs21\\f4\\fs24\\b reactivation (post-primary) pulmonary tuberculosis\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\b  involving the upper lobes, more on the right side.,Active cavitary disease likely \\par\\par\\par clinical and microbiological correlation AFB smear is advised \\plain\\f5\\fs22\\b\\line\\line\\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 13, '2024-06-12 05:56:28');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('lt cxr inf ', '<p><font face="Arial">X-ray report of Chest P/A View: </font></p><p align="center"><font face="Arial"> </font></p><table border="0" cellspacing="0" dir="ltr" width="787">	<tbody>		<tr>			<td valign="middle" width="23%">			<p><font face="Arial">Diaphragm </font></p>			</td>			<td valign="middle" width="4%">			<p><font face="Arial">: </font></p>			</td>			<td valign="middle" width="73%">			<p><font face="Arial">left hemidiaphragm is not well delineated .</font></p>			</td>		</tr>		<tr>			<td valign="middle" width="23%">			<p><font face="Arial">Costophrenic angle </font></p>			</td>			<td valign="middle" width="4%">			<p><font face="Arial">: </font></p>			</td>			<td valign="middle" width="73%">			<p><font face="Arial">left is blunt .</font></p>			</td>		</tr>		<tr>			<td valign="middle" width="23%">			<p><font face="Arial">Lung </font></p>			</td>			<td valign="middle" width="4%">			<p><font face="Arial">: </font></p>			</td>			<td valign="middle" width="73%">			<p><font face="Arial">Ill-defined opacity is noted inleft </font></p>			</td>		</tr>		<tr>			<td valign="middle" width="23%">			<p><font face="Arial">Heart </font></p>			</td>			<td valign="middle" width="4%">			<p><font face="Arial">: </font></p>			</td>			<td valign="middle" width="73%">			<p><font face="Arial">Normal in transverse diameter. </font></p>			</td>		</tr>		<tr>			<td valign="middle" width="23%">			<p><font face="Arial">Bony thorax </font></p>			</td>			<td valign="middle" width="4%">			<p><font face="Arial">: </font></p>			</td>			<td valign="middle" width="73%">			<p><font face="Arial">No fracture or any bony lesion is seen. </font></p>			</td>		</tr>	</tbody></table><p><font face="Arial"> </font></p><p><font face="Arial">Impression:Left sided pulmonary inflammatory lesion. </font></p><p><font face="Arial"><img height="75" src="http://teleradbangladesh.selfip.com/Image1.gif" width="174" /></font></p>', 'html', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 13, '2024-06-12 05:56:28');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('    RGU & MCU ', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff1{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\fswiss\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Calibri;}\r\n{\\f2\\fnil\\fcharset1\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f3\\fnil\\fcharset1\\fprq2 Cambria;}\r\n{\\f4\\froman\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Times New Roman;}\r\n{\\f5\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;\\red27\\green27\\blue27;\\red245\\green255\\blue240;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\widctlpar\\sa200\\sl276\\slmult1\\f1\\fs22 Normal;}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}{\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\*\\cs17\\b\\additive\\sbasedon10 STRONG;}{\\s18\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f2\\fs24\\sbasedon16 BODY;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12000\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f0\\fs24                              RGU & MCU \\par\\par\\par Control film : No radio opaque calculus is noted in the bladder region and in the line of urethra.  \\par RGU :\\par\\par The anterior urethra is well opacified by the contrast media. No abnormal dilatation, narrowing or filling defect is noted.    \\par MCU :\\par\\par   Urinary bladder is well outlined by the contrast media. No intravesical filling defect is noted. \\par No vesico ureteric reflux is noted.\\par Posterior urethra is opacified with contrast media and normal in course and calibre.\\par Post voidal film: significant residual urine.\\par\\par Comments:  Significant PVR\\par\\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\sl276\\slmult1\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f1\\fs32\\b\\ul CHEST X-RAY AP VIEW:\\par\\trowd\\irow0\\irowband0\\trgaph56\\trleft0\\trftsWidth1\\trftsWidthB3\\trftsWidthA3\\trpaddl56\\trpaddt56\\trpaddr56\\trpaddb56\\trpaddfl3\\trpaddft3\\trpaddfr3\\trpaddfb3\\clvertalc\\clbrdrt\\brdrs\\brdrw15\\clcbpat4\\clftsWidth3\\clwWidth11016\\cellx11016\\pard\\s18\\intbl\\widctlpar\\plain\\cs17\\f2\\fs24\\b\\cf3 Endotracheal tubes\\cell\\row\\trowd\\irow1\\irowband1\\lastrow\\trgaph56\\trleft0\\trftsWidth1\\trftsWidthB3\\trftsWidthA3\\trpaddl56\\trpaddt56\\trpaddr56\\trpaddb56\\trpaddfl3\\trpaddft3\\trpaddfr3\\trpaddfb3\\clvertalc\\clbrdrb\\brdrs\\brdrw15\\clcbpat4\\clftsWidth3\\clwWidth11016\\cellx11016\\pard\\s18\\intbl\\widctlpar\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\cf3 Safe level 5 cm from carina (T4-T5 interspace), minimum distance 2 cm\\cell\\row\\pard\\s18\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f3\\fs26\\cf3\\par\\trowd\\irow0\\irowband0\\trgaph56\\trleft0\\trftsWidth1\\trftsWidthB3\\trftsWidthA3\\trpaddl56\\trpaddt56\\trpaddr56\\trpaddb56\\trpaddfl3\\trpaddft3\\trpaddfr3\\trpaddfb3\\clvertalc\\clbrdrt\\brdrs\\brdrw15\\clcbpat4\\clftsWidth3\\clwWidth11016\\cellx11016\\pard\\s18\\intbl\\widctlpar\\plain\\cs17\\f2\\fs24\\b\\cf3 Nasogastric tube\\cell\\row\\trowd\\irow1\\irowband1\\trgaph56\\trleft0\\trftsWidth1\\trftsWidthB3\\trftsWidthA3\\trpaddl56\\trpaddt56\\trpaddr56\\trpaddb56\\trpaddfl3\\trpaddft3\\trpaddfr3\\trpaddfb3\\clvertalc\\clbrdrb\\brdrs\\brdrw15\\clcbpat4\\clftsWidth3\\clwWidth11016\\cellx11016\\pard\\s18\\intbl\\widctlpar\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\cf3 Ideally the distal duodenum\\cell\\row\\trowd\\irow2\\irowband2\\trgaph56\\trleft0\\trftsWidth1\\trftsWidthB3\\trftsWidthA3\\trpaddl56\\trpaddt56\\trpaddr56\\trpaddb56\\trpaddfl3\\trpaddft3\\trpaddfr3\\trpaddfb3\\clvertalc\\clbrdrt\\brdrs\\brdrw15\\clcbpat4\\clftsWidth3\\clwWidth11016\\cellx11016\\pard\\s18\\intbl\\widctlpar\\plain\\cs17\\f2\\fs24\\b\\cf3 CVP lines\\cell\\row\\trowd\\irow3\\irowband3\\trgaph56\\trleft0\\trftsWidth1\\trftsWidthB3\\trftsWidthA3\\trpaddl56\\trpaddt56\\trpaddr56\\trpaddb56\\trpaddfl3\\trpaddft3\\trpaddfr3\\trpaddfb3\\clvertalc\\clcbpat4\\clftsWidth3\\clwWidth11016\\cellx11016\\pard\\s18\\intbl\\widctlpar\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\cf3 Ideally placed between proximal venous valves of the subclavian or jugular veins and the right atrium. Jugular venous placement has lower complications.\\cell\\row\\trowd\\irow4\\irowband4\\trgaph56\\trleft0\\trftsWidth1\\trftsWidthB3\\trftsWidthA3\\trpaddl56\\trpaddt56\\trpaddr56\\trpaddb56\\trpaddfl3\\trpaddft3\\trpaddfr3\\trpaddfb3\\clvertalc\\clcbpat4\\clftsWidth3\\clwWidth11016\\cellx11016\\pard\\s18\\intbl\\widctlpar\\plain\\cs17\\f2\\fs24\\b\\cf3 Swan ganz catheter\\cell\\row\\trowd\\irow5\\irowband5\\trgaph56\\trleft0\\trftsWidth1\\trftsWidthB3\\trftsWidthA3\\trpaddl56\\trpaddt56\\trpaddr56\\trpaddb56\\trpaddfl3\\trpaddft3\\trpaddfr3\\trpaddfb3\\clvertalc\\clcbpat4\\clftsWidth3\\clwWidth11016\\cellx11016\\pard\\s18\\intbl\\widctlpar\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\cf3 The tip is wedged into the distal pulmonary artery.\\cell\\row\\trowd\\irow6\\irowband6\\trgaph56\\trleft0\\trftsWidth1\\trftsWidthB3\\trftsWidthA3\\trpaddl56\\trpaddt56\\trpaddr56\\trpaddb56\\trpaddfl3\\trpaddft3\\trpaddfr3\\trpaddfb3\\clvertalc\\clcbpat4\\clftsWidth3\\clwWidth11016\\cellx11016\\pard\\s18\\intbl\\widctlpar The balloon is deflated once the pressure is taken, and the tip is pulled back to the main pulmonary artery.\\cell\\row\\trowd\\irow7\\irowband7\\trgaph56\\trleft0\\trftsWidth1\\trftsWidthB3\\trftsWidthA3\\trpaddl56\\trpaddt56\\trpaddr56\\trpaddb56\\trpaddfl3\\trpaddft3\\trpaddfr3\\trpaddfb3\\clvertalc\\clcbpat4\\clftsWidth3\\clwWidth11016\\cellx11016\\pard\\s18\\intbl\\widctlpar The tip of the catheter located within the mediastinal shadow indicates correct placement.\\cell\\row\\trowd\\irow8\\irowband8\\trgaph56\\trleft0\\trftsWidth1\\trftsWidthB3\\trftsWidthA3\\trpaddl56\\trpaddt56\\trpaddr56\\trpaddb56\\trpaddfl3\\trpaddft3\\trpaddfr3\\trpaddfb3\\clvertalc\\clcbpat4\\clftsWidth3\\clwWidth11016\\cellx11016\\pard\\s18\\intbl\\widctlpar\\plain\\cs17\\f2\\fs24\\b\\cf3 The thoracostomy tube\\cell\\row\\trowd\\irow9\\irowband9\\trgaph56\\trleft0\\trftsWidth1\\trftsWidthB3\\trftsWidthA3\\trpaddl56\\trpaddt56\\trpaddr56\\trpaddb56\\trpaddfl3\\trpaddft3\\trpaddfr3\\trpaddfb3\\clvertalc\\clcbpat4\\clftsWidth3\\clwWidth11016\\cellx11016\\pard\\s18\\intbl\\widctlpar\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\cf3 The last side-hole in a thoracostomy tube can be identified by an interruption in the radiopaque line.\\cell\\row\\trowd\\irow10\\irowband10\\lastrow\\trgaph56\\trleft0\\trftsWidth1\\trftsWidthB3\\trftsWidthA3\\trpaddl56\\trpaddt56\\trpaddr56\\trpaddb56\\trpaddfl3\\trpaddft3\\trpaddfr3\\trpaddfb3\\clvertalc\\clbrdrb\\brdrs\\brdrw15\\clcbpat4\\clftsWidth3\\clwWidth11016\\cellx11016\\pard\\s18\\intbl\\widctlpar This interruption in the radiopaque line should lie within the thoracic cavity, if not and or with evidence of subcutaneous air, a misplaced tube is suspected.\\cell\\row\\pard\\s18\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f3\\fs26\\cf3\\par\\plain\\f3\\fs26\\cf3\\cb4\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat4 The tip of the cardiac pacemaker should be at the apex of the heart, and there should be no sharp angulations along the length of the pacemaker wires.\\plain\\f2\\fs24  \\par\\plain\\f3\\fs26\\cf3\\cb4\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat4 A tip that appears to be placed beyond the epicardial fat stripe may have perforated the myocardium.\\plain\\f2\\fs24  \\par\\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f1\\fs28 Trachea is central in position.\\par Diaphragm is normal in position, contour and definition.\\par Heart  size  is not measured   as it appears enlarged  in transverse diameter  in AP film.\\par Bronchovascular markings are accentuated in both the lungs  \\par Both basal angles are clear.\\par Bony thorax is unremarkable.\\par\\par\\plain\\f1\\fs28\\b\\ul Comments:\\plain\\f1\\fs28\\b  Suggestive