tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f7\\fs22\\b\\ul X-Ray Left hand  B/V\\par arthropathies of hand , \\par\\plain\\f7\\fs22\\b gout    mtp\\par psoriasis    pip and dip and pissiform sparing pip of thumb  \\par rheumatoid     mip and pip joints plus pissiform ulnar styloid  dip of thumb \\par osteoarthritis  pip dip ...2  to 5 \\par dip of thumb ,base of 1st metatarsal and medial carpal bones \\par erosive   d ip ,pip  joints  sparing pip of thumb  plus base of 1st metatarsal \\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f8\\fs20\\\'b7\\tab}\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\fi-360\\li360\\tx360\\ls1\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls1\\pnstart1\\pnf8\\pnfs20\\pnb\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}\\plain\\f5\\fs20\\cf5\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6 An intra-articular fracture at the base of the thumb metacarpal is called a\\loch\\f5\\hich\\f5\\~\\plain\\cs20\\f5\\fs20\\cf7\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6{\\txfielddef{\\*\\txfieldstart\\txfieldtype1\\txfieldflags0}{\\*\\txfielddatadef\\txfielddatatype1\\txfielddata 680074007400700073003a002f002f0072006100640069006f007000610065006400690061002e006f00720067002f00610072007400690063006c00650073002f00620065006e006e006500740074002d00660072006100630074007500720065000000}{\\*\\txfieldtext Bennett\'s fracture{\\*\\txfieldend}}{\\field{\\*\\fldinst{ HYPERLINK "https://radiopaedia.org/articles/bennett-fracture" }}{\\fldrslt{Bennett\'s fracture}}}}\\plain\\f5\\fs20\\cf5\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6 .\\plain\\f4\\fs24  \\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f8\\fs20\\\'b7\\tab}\\ls1\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls1\\pnstart1\\pnf8\\pnfs20\\pnb0\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}\\plain\\f5\\fs20\\cf5\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6 A\\loch\\f5\\hich\\f5\\~\\plain\\cs20\\f5\\fs20\\cf7\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6{\\txfielddef{\\*\\txfieldstart\\txfieldtype1\\txfieldflags0}{\\*\\txfielddatadef\\txfielddatatype1\\txfielddata 680074007400700073003a002f002f0072006100640069006f007000610065006400690061002e006f00720067002f00610072007400690063006c00650073002f0072006f006c0061006e0064006f002d00660072006100630074007500720065000000}{\\*\\txfieldtext Rolando fracture{\\*\\txfieldend}}{\\field{\\*\\fldinst{ HYPERLINK "https://radiopaedia.org/articles/rolando-fracture" }}{\\fldrslt{Rolando fracture}}}}\\plain\\f5\\fs20\\cf5\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6\\loch\\f5\\hich\\f5\\~is a comminuted intra-articular fracture-dislocation of the base of the thumb (base of the 1st\\~\\plain\\cs20\\f5\\fs20\\cf7\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6{\\txfielddef{\\*\\txfieldstart\\txfieldtype1\\txfieldflags0}{\\*\\txfielddatadef\\txfielddatatype1\\txfielddata 680074007400700073003a002f002f0072006100640069006f007000610065006400690061002e006f00720067002f00610072007400690063006c00650073002f006d00650074006100630061007200700061006c002d0062006f006e00650073002d0031000000}{\\*\\txfieldtext metacarpal{\\*\\txfieldend}}{\\field{\\*\\fldinst{ HYPERLINK "https://radiopaedia.org/articles/metacarpal-bones-1" }}{\\fldrslt{metacarpal}}}}\\plain\\f5\\fs20\\cf5\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6 ). Simply put, it is a comminuted\\loch\\f5\\hich\\f5\\~\\plain\\cs20\\f5\\fs20\\cf7\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6{\\txfielddef{\\*\\txfieldstart\\txfieldtype1\\txfieldflags0}{\\*\\txfielddatadef\\txfielddatatype1\\txfielddata 680074007400700073003a002f002f0072006100640069006f007000610065006400690061002e006f00720067002f00610072007400690063006c00650073002f00620065006e006e006500740074002d00660072006100630074007500720065000000}{\\*\\txfieldtext Bennett fractur{\\*\\txfieldend}}{\\field{\\*\\fldinst{ HYPERLINK "https://radiopaedia.org/articles/bennett-fracture" }}{\\fldrslt{Bennett fractur}}}}\\plain\\f4\\fs24  \\plain\\f5\\fs20\\cf5\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6 The fracture line is typically T or Y-shaped. The volar fragment remains attached to the carpometacarpal joint, w\\plain\\f4\\fs24  \\par{\\pntext\\pard\\plain\\f8\\fs20\\\'b7\\tab}\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\fi-360\\li360\\sa109\\tx360\\ls1\\ilvl0{\\*\\pn\\pnlvlblt\\ilvl0\\ls1\\pnstart1\\pnf8\\pnfs20\\pnb0\\pni0\\pnstrike0\\pnulnone\\pncf0\\pncb0{\\pntxtb \\\'b7}}\\plain\\f5\\fs20\\cf5\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6 Fracture in the base of the first metacarpal without intraarticular extension(pseudo-\\plain\\cs20\\f5\\fs20\\cf7\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6{\\txfielddef{\\*\\txfieldstart\\txfieldtype1\\txfieldflags0}{\\*\\txfielddatadef\\txfielddatatype1\\txfielddata 680074007400700073003a002f002f0072006100640069006f007000610065006400690061002e006f00720067002f00610072007400690063006c00650073002f0065007000690062006100730061006c002d00660072006100630074007500720065002d006f0066002d007400680065002d007400680075006d0062000000}{\\*\\txfieldtext Bennett\\loch\\f5\\hich\\f5\\~{\\*\\txfieldend}}{\\field{\\*\\fldinst{ HYPERLINK "https://radiopaedia.org/articles/epibasal-fracture-of-the-thumb" }}{\\fldrslt{Bennett\\loch\\f5\\hich\\f5\\~}}}}\\plain\\f5\\fs20\\cf5\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6 fracture).\\par\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sa109 The most common pattern of thumb fractures is extraarticular epibasal fracture.\\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f7\\fs22\\b Fracture is  seen in the 2nd and 3rd  metacarpals \\plain\\f7\\fs12\\par\\plain\\f7\\fs22 Articular margin is not involved.\\par\\plain\\f7\\fs12\\par\\plain\\f7\\fs22 Overlying soft tissue is swollen\\par\\plain\\f7\\fs12\\par\\plain\\f7\\fs22 Joint spaces are normal\\par\\plain\\f7\\fs18\\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f7\\fs22\\b\\ul Comment\\plain\\f7\\fs22\\b : Fracture of the \\plain\\f1\\fs22  \\plain\\f7\\fs22\\b  2nd and 3rd  metacarpals \\plain\\f7\\fs12\\par\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sb134\\sa134\\plain\\f4\\fs24 There is a fracture noted at the \\plain\\cs21\\f4\\fs24 base of the first metacarpal bone\\plain\\f4\\fs24 .The fractu