 }\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qr\\plain\\f0\\fs24{\\txfielddef{\\*\\txfieldstart\\txfieldtype3\\txfieldflags0}{\\*\\txfielddatadef\\txfielddatatype3\\txfielddata 00030001}{\\*\\txfieldtext 1{\\*\\txfieldend}}{\\field{\\*\\fldinst{ PAGE \\\\* Arabic }}{\\fldrslt{1}}}}\\plain\\f0\\fs24{\\txfielddef{\\*\\txfieldstart\\txfieldtype0\\txfieldflags0}{\\*\\txfieldtext  of {\\*\\txfieldend}} of }\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qr\\plain\\f0\\fs24{\\txfielddef{\\*\\txfieldstart\\txfieldtype0\\txfieldflags0}{\\*\\txfieldtext 1{\\*\\txfieldend}}1}\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qr\\par}\\pard\\s17\\itap0\\keepn\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f2\\fs28\\b\\ul RT. FEMUR   B/V:\\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\par\\pard\\s17\\itap0\\keepn\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\b\\ul FINDINGS:\\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f2\\fs28\\par\\plain\\f2\\fs28\\b\\i\\ul Fractures   with periosteal reactions are seen at the mid shaft of right femur with orthopaedic hardware of internal fixation are seen in situ \\par\\plain\\f2\\fs28\\par Joints spaces are normal. \\par\\par Articular margins are regular in out line. \\par Bird\'s beak appearance of femur epiphysis with shallow acetabulum ,TB \\par\\pard\\s18\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f4\\fs20\\cf4\\cb5\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat5 There is a poorly defined erosion at the lateral aspect of the right femoral head/neck junction, with poorly visualized cortical margins along the axial aspect of the femoral head and acetabulum. Mild juxtarticular osteopenia is also noted on the right. The gluteal, capsular and psoas fat pads are markedly distorted on the right, indicating a large joint effusion.\\par\\plain\\f4\\fs20\\cf4\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6\\loch\\f4\\hich\\f4\\~tuberculous arthritis, demonstrating\\~\\plain\\cs19\\f4\\fs20\\cf7\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6{\\txfielddef{\\*\\txfieldstart\\txfieldtype1\\txfieldflags0}{\\*\\txfielddatadef\\txfielddatatype1\\txfielddata 680074007400700073003a002f002f0072006100640069006f007000610065006400690061002e006f00720067002f00610072007400690063006c00650073002f007000680065006d00690073007400650072002d00740072006900610064002d0074007500620065007200630075006c006f007300690073003f006c0061006e0067003d00750073000000}{\\*\\txfieldtext Phemister triad{\\*\\txfieldend}}{\\field{\\*\\fldinst{ HYPERLINK "https://radiopaedia.org/articles/phemister-triad-tuberculosis?lang=us" }}{\\fldrslt{Phemister triad}}}}\\plain\\f4\\fs20\\cf4\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6\\loch\\f4\\hich\\f4\\~with a marginal erosion at the lateral femoral head neck junction, juxta-articular osteopenia and late loss of joint space.\\plain\\f4\\fs20\\cf4\\cb5\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat5\\loch\\f4\\hich\\f4\\~\\plain\\f3\\fs24  \\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f2\\fs32\\b\\par\\pard\\s18\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f4\\fs20\\cf4\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6\\loch\\f4\\hich\\f4\\~in contrast to\\~\\plain\\cs19\\f4\\fs20\\cf7\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6{\\txfielddef{\\*\\txfieldstart\\txfieldtype1\\txfieldflags0}{\\*\\txfielddatadef\\txfielddatatype1\\txfielddata 680074007400700073003a002f002f0072006100640069006f007000610065006400690061002e006f00720067002f00610072007400690063006c00650073002f007300650070007400690063002d006100720074006800720069007400690073003f006c0061006e0067003d00750073000000}{\\*\\txfieldtext pyogenic arthritis{\\*\\txfieldend}}{\\field{\\*\\fldinst{ HYPERLINK "https://radiopaedia.org/articles/septic-arthritis?lang=us" }}{\\fldrslt{pyogenic arthritis}}}}\\plain\\f4\\fs20\\cf4\\cb6\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat6 , the development of bone ankylosis is uncommon in tuberculous arthritis and, when present, is more likely to be secondary to prior surgical intervention\\plain\\f3\\fs24  \\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f2\\fs36\\b Comment: Tuberculous arthritis .\\par\\tab\\tab As per description .\\plain\\f4\\fs22  \\par\\pard\\s18\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f3\\fs24 Osteosarcoma of the distal fibula-predominantly osteoblas tic. Amorphous calcification/ossification is present in the soft tissues with cortical destruction and a little periosteal new bone formation \\par an eccentric area of permeative hone destruction in the metadiaphysis adjacent to the knee joint, associated with cortical erosion and a well-defined soft tissue mass. Elevation of the periosteum is associated with new bone formation, the so-called Codman\'s triangles. The epiphysis usually appears normal. The soft-tissue mass may contain calcific tion that may show either an amorphous or a spiculated appearance.together with sclerosis in the shaft of the bone, surrounding the lesion. bulk. Careful delineation of the lesion and assessment of relation A mixture of sclerosis and bone destruction is usually present within the bony lesion. Occasionally the lesion may be purely lytic \\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 13, '2023-11-23 14:47:45');
