tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f6\\fs21\\b\\i\\cf3 Dr.Self  \\plain\\f2\\fs24\\cell\\row\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par}\r\n{\\footerf\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f0\\fs24\\par\\pard\\s18\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f3\\fs16\\cf3 N.B. : This is only a professional opinion and not the final diagnosis. Radiological investigations are subject to variations due to technical limitations. Hence, correlation with clinical findings and other investigations should be carried out to know true nature of illness. This report is not for medico-legal use.\\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qr\\plain\\f3\\fs16\\cf3{\\txfielddef{\\*\\txfieldstart\\txfieldtype0\\txfieldflags0}{\\*\\txfieldtext Page: {\\*\\txfieldend}}Page: }\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qr\\plain\\f3\\fs16\\cf3{\\txfielddef{\\*\\txfieldstart\\txfieldtype3\\txfieldflags0}{\\*\\txfielddatadef\\txfielddatatype3\\txfielddata 00030001}{\\*\\txfieldtext 1{\\*\\txfieldend}}{\\field{\\*\\fldinst{ PAGE \\\\* Arabic }}{\\fldrslt{1}}}}\\plain\\f3\\fs16\\cf3{\\txfielddef{\\*\\txfieldstart\\txfieldtype0\\txfieldflags0}{\\*\\txfieldtext  of {\\*\\txfieldend}} of }\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qr\\plain\\f3\\fs16\\cf3{\\txfielddef{\\*\\txfieldstart\\txfieldtype0\\txfieldflags0}{\\*\\txfieldtext 1{\\*\\txfieldend}}1}\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\qr\\par}\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f1\\fs28\\b\\ul LUMBO-SACRAL SPINE B/V:\\par\\plain\\f1\\fs28 Lumbar lordotic curvature is straightened \\par\\pard\\s19\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sb134\\sa134\\plain\\f4\\fs24 There is \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 collapse of the L1 vertebral body\\plain\\f4\\fs24 , with \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 loss of vertebral height\\plain\\f4\\fs24 , more pronounced \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 anteriorly\\plain\\f4\\fs24 , resulting in \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 wedging deformity\\plain\\f4\\fs24 .\\line The \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 superior endplate\\plain\\f4\\fs24  appears irregular\\line No obvious \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 retropulsion of bony fragments\\plain\\f4\\fs24  into the spinal canal is seen on X-ray\\par  The \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 posterior elements\\plain\\f4\\fs24  appear intact.\\line\\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 Adjacent intervertebral disc spaces\\plain\\f4\\fs24  are maintained.\\line No other vertebral fractures are seen in the visualized region.\\line\\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 Paravertebral soft tissues\\plain\\f4\\fs24  appear normal.\\line\\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24\\b\\ul Impression:\\par\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\line\\par\\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 Traumatic collapse/ fracture of L1 vertebral body.\\par\\plain\\f4\\fs24\\line Suggest \\plain\\cs20\\f4\\fs24 MRI correlation\\plain\\f4\\fs24  to assess for canal compromise or associated soft tissue injury.\\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 13, '2024-07-09 12:03:29');
INSERT INTO `t_templates` (`name`, `content`, `template_type`, `modalityList`, `user`, `templateImpressionData`, `templateNodeID`, `passwordReSetTime`) VALUES ('abd  fcpd ', '{\\rtf1\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\uc1\\deff1{\\fonttbl\r\n{\\f0\\fnil\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f1\\fswiss\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Calibri;}\r\n{\\f2\\fnil\\fcharset1\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f3\\fscript\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Comic Sans MS;}\r\n{\\f4\\fswiss\\fcharset0\\fprq2 Arial;}\r\n{\\f5\\froman\\fcharset2\\fprq2 Symbol;}}\r\n{\\colortbl;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;\\red51\\green51\\blue51;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;}\r\n{\\stylesheet{\\s0\\itap0\\widctlpar\\f1\\fs22 Normal;}{\\*\\cs10\\additive Default Paragraph Font;}{\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f0\\fs24 [Normal];}{\\s17\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\f2\\fs24\\sbasedon16 BODY;}{\\s18\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\sb93\\sa186\\f1\\fs28\\b\\sbasedon17 H3;}{\\*\\cs19\\b\\additive\\sbasedon10 STRONG;}}\r\n{\\*\\generator TX_RTF32 16.0.533.500;}\r\n\\deftab1134\\paperw12000\\paperh15840\\margl1440\\margt1440\\margr1440\\margb1440\\widowctrl\\formshade\\sectd\r\n\\headery720\\footery720\\pgwsxn12240\\pghsxn15840\\marglsxn1440\\margtsxn1440\\margrsxn1440\\margbsxn1440\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f3\\fs28\\b\\ul X-Ray Abdomen AP view\\plain\\f3\\fs22\\b\\ul\\par\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\b Findings: \\par\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\par\\pard\\s17\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\tab\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f3\\fs28\\tab\\plain\\f3\\fs24 A biliary stent is seen in situ .No pneumobilia is seen \\par\\plain\\f3\\fs28\\b Multiple different sizes calcifications are noted located along the region of pancreatic duct\\plain\\f3\\fs28 .\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\par\\par\\pard\\s17\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\b\\i\\ul\\cf3\\cb4\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat4 Loops of gas-filled bowel are not dilated but seem to be clumped centrally in the abdomen. \\par Elsewhere there is hazy increased density.\\loch\\f2\\hich\\f2\\~\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\b\\i\\ul  \\par\\par\\pard\\s18\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f2\\fs34\\b\\cf5\\cb4\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat4\\par\\pard\\s17\\itap0\\nowidctlpar\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\cf3\\cb4\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat4 The large bowel is massively dilated, the caecal pole is displaced and the right iliac fossa (\\plain\\cs19\\f4\\fs24\\b\\cf3\\cb4\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat4 RIF\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\cf3\\cb4\\chshdng0\\chcfpat0\\chcbpat4 ) is devoid of bowel gas. These are typical appearances of caecal volvulus.\\par\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\b\\i Cicumferential irregular narrowing of terminal illeum is noted with vertical orientation and smooth trapering .\\par\\plain\\f2\\fs24\\par Ceacum contracted ,deformed and high up .\\par Suggestive of illeoceacal TB.\\par\\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\tab No free gas shadow is seen.\\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\li720\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080 No abnormal air-fluid level or soft tissue shadow is seen. \\par Normal pattern of the bowel gas distribution is noted.\\par No calculi or calcification noted along the KUB region. \\par\\par\\pard\\itap0\\widctlpar\\tx720\\tx1440\\tx2160\\tx2880\\tx3600\\tx4320\\tx5040\\tx5760\\tx6480\\tx7200\\tx7920\\tx8640\\tx9360\\tx10080\\plain\\f3\\fs24\\b IMPRESSION: \\par\\pard\\s16\\itap0\\nowidctlpar Pancreatic calculi .\\par SUGGESTIVE OF ASCITES \\par SUGGESTIVE OF CAECAL VOLVULUS \\par\\par }', 'rtf', '[]', 'drrizwana', NULL, 13, '2024-09-30 13:38:32');
